# There was no .gitignore at all until 2026-10-01, so simply RUNNING the app in a checkout left
# __pycache__/ everywhere and `--diagnose` left diagnostic_report.txt in the repo root — and a build left
# build/ and dist/. That matters more here than in most repos: Morpheus compiles this project from its own
# copy of the files and pushes them to GitHub, so anything that lands in the working tree can end up
# committed, and a committed .venv or dist/ is hundreds of megabytes.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Build output — build.py writes both, and neither belongs in the repository
build/
dist/
*.spec

# What --diagnose writes next to the source when the app is not frozen (config.get_base_dir)
diagnostic_report.txt

# The app's own scratch
crash_log.txt
*.log

.DS_Store
